        "original_id": "45a5cec6-af44-55e0-a370-e45cacf71749",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: St. John's College, Belize\n- People: Jorge Espat\n- Places: Belize City, Tobacco Caye, Dangriga, Belize\n- Concepts: Liberal arts education\n- Topics: Liberal arts subjects, academic divisions\n\nFacts:\n- Liberal arts education traditionally centered on grammar, logic, and rhetoric, with arithmetic, geometry, music theory, and astronomy also included.\n- St. John's College in Belize offers liberal arts and science courses through three divisions at the secondary, British A-level, and United States junior college levels.\n- Jorge Espat served on the faculty of St. John's College in Belize City as an instructor and later as president.\n- Tobacco Caye is a small island in Belize located about 10 miles east of Dangriga.",
